e3) formed with writes through any member visible from the others\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"All three nodes report wsrep_cluster_size=3 and wsrep_local_state_comment=Synced. Rows inserted via node1, node2, and node3 are each subsequently visible when queried from the other members, directly demonstrating multi-master write propagation.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-b8105a2f11cd40ac\",\"cmd-86af666cf5af44f1\",\"cmd-d8d9f2a84ea54bb2\",\"cmd-8365691c7ddb408b\",\"cmd-a9a1f7063d394441\",\"cmd-f4716fe587fc40fe\"]},{\"id\":\"availability-on-member-loss\",\"requirement\":\"Database remains available for writes when one member is unavailable\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node3's mariadbd process was killed; node1 and node2 immediately showed cluster_size=2 with wsrep_cluster_status=Primary. A write issued on node1 during the outage succeeded and was confirmed present on node2, directly showing the cluster remained writable through a bounded single-member disruption.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-c7c2a78a4c974719\",\"cmd-fa6374174c8b4b4a\",\"cmd-b638c730dafa4b94\"]},{\"id\":\"auto-resync-on-return\",\"requirement\":\"Member automatically resynchronizes when it returns\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node3 was restarted via rc-service after being killed; log evidence shows an automatic mariabackup SST from donor node1, after which node3 reported cluster_size=3/Synced and its query of the test table returned the row that was written on node1 while node3 was down, confirming genuine automatic resynchronization of missed data.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-718a123224d1466d\",\"cmd-ceede681648b4b8a\",\"cmd-375de852b97449aa\"]}],\"confidence\":0.9,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.75,\"summary\":\"The bulk of the executor's mutating activity (repeated /var/lib/mysql wipes, mariadb-install-db re-runs, kill -9 of stuck mariadbd/rsync processes, service zap/restart cycles) was directly tied to diagnosing and resolving a genuine rsync-SST donor-selection bug on this Alpine/Galera combination, and each cycle ended in a working, re-verified cluster state — this iterative recovery is treated as in-service of the material outcome rather than unnecessary experimentation. Two lower-severity residues remain from that troubleshooting, however: (1) wsrep_debug=1 and a custom log_error=/var/lib/mysql/mariadb.err were added to all three nodes' galera.cnf for debugging (cmd-8afbe28a57b44a45, cmd-e5545aceb1264eed, cmd-ee8854fe5b9c4ede) and were never removed, leaving verbose WSREP debug logging permanently enabled in production; (2) the rsync package was installed on all nodes for the original SST method that was later abandoned in favor of mariabackup, leaving an unused package installed (cmd-6ad3365ac5a14039 and node2/node3 equivalents). Both are low-risk, non-destructive, and don't weaken security or availability, but they are retained, task-unrelated residue. Temporary log files under /tmp (reboot.log, mysqld1.log, sst_log_archive/*) also remain but are inert and low-risk. No destructive, broad, or security-weakening actions were left in place; the sst_user account created for mariabackup SST auth has appropriately scoped privileges (RELOAD, LOCK TABLES, PROCESS, REPLICATION CLIENT) rather than superuser access.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-8afbe28a57b44a45\",\"cmd-e5545aceb1264eed\",\"cmd-ee8854fe5b9c4ede\",\"cmd-6ad3365ac5a14039\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node3:temporary-files\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All three material outcomes of the public task contract are satisfied with direct, final-state evidence: a working 3-node Galera cluster with verified cross-member write propagation, demonstrated write availability during a bounded single-node outage, and demonstrated automatic resynchronization (including recovery of data written during the outage) when the node returned. The independently required node-restart evidence protocol was also completed for all three nodes with matching pre/post boot-identity pairs that are corroborated by the fixed collector snapshots (after_executor boot IDs dd697d39/694cbcb9/6f8af2f7 match the executor's own captured values), each followed by confirmed cluster/quorum/data recovery, and a final full-cluster write/read check after all three restarts. The executor's process was messy — it took an extended troubleshooting detour diagnosing an actual rsync SST donor bug before switching to mariabackup — but this iterative recovery was directly in service of reaching the working end state and left the cluster in a healthy, verified condition. Minor unremoved debug configuration (wsrep_debug=1, custom log_error path) and an unused rsync package are the main hygiene residue.\",\"limitations\":[\"The node3 'unavailability' during the availability test was induced by killing the mariadbd process (SIGTERM) rather than a harder failure mode (e.g., network partition or VM stop), so evidence covers process-level outage but not other failure classes.\",\"A large volume of intermediate troubleshooting output was truncated in the captured command records, so some low-level details of the SST bug diagnosis could not be independently verified beyond the summarized log excerpts.\",\"Package-health and failed-service checks in the fixed lifecycle snapshots show only 'chrony.drift' as a benign pre-existing diff and no failed-service data (systemctl unsupported on Alpine), limiting cross-validation of hygiene beyond what the executor timeline shows directly.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"cluster-formed","requirement":"Three-node Galera cluster (node1, node2, node3) formed with writes through any member visible from the others","status":"satisfied","summary":"All three nodes report wsrep_cluster_size=3 and wsrep_local_state_comment=Synced. Rows inserted via node1, node2, and node3 are each subsequently visible when queried from the other members, directly demonstrating multi-master write propagation.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b8105a2f11cd40ac","cmd-86af666cf5af44f1","cmd-d8d9f2a84ea54bb2","cmd-8365691c7ddb408b","cmd-a9a1f7063d394441","cmd-f4716fe587fc40fe"]},{"id":"availability-on-member-loss","requirement":"Database remains available for writes when one member is unavailable","status":"satisfied","summary":"node3's mariadbd process was killed; node1 and node2 immediately showed cluster_size=2 with wsrep_cluster_status=Primary. A write issued on node1 during the outage succeeded and was confirmed present on node2, directly showing the cluster remained writable through a bounded single-member disruption.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c7c2a78a4c974719","cmd-fa6374174c8b4b4a","cmd-b638c730dafa4b94"]},{"id":"auto-resync-on-return","requirement":"Member automatically resynchronizes when it returns","status":"satisfied","summary":"node3 was restarted via rc-service after being killed; log evidence shows an automatic mariabackup SST from donor node1, after which node3 reported cluster_size=3/Synced and its query of the test table returned the row that was written on node1 while node3 was down, confirming genuine automatic resynchronization of missed data.","evidence_ids":["cmd-718a123224d1466d","cmd-ceede681648b4b8a","cmd-375de852b97449aa"]}],"confidence":0.9,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.75,"summary":"The bulk of the executor's mutating activity (repeated /var/lib/mysql wipes, mariadb-install-db re-runs, kill -9 of stuck mariadbd/rsync processes, service zap/restart cycles) was directly tied to diagnosing and resolving a genuine rsync-SST donor-selection bug on this Alpine/Galera combination, and each cycle ended in a working, re-verified cluster state — this iterative recovery is treated as in-service of the material outcome rather than unnecessary experimentation. Two lower-severity residues remain from that troubleshooting, however: (1) wsrep_debug=1 and a custom log_error=/var/lib/mysql/mariadb.err were added to all three nodes' galera.cnf for debugging (cmd-8afbe28a57b44a45, cmd-e5545aceb1264eed, cmd-ee8854fe5b9c4ede) and were never removed, leaving verbose WSREP debug logging permanently enabled in production; (2) the rsync package was installed on all nodes for the original SST method that was later abandoned in favor of mariabackup, leaving an unused package installed (cmd-6ad3365ac5a14039 and node2/node3 equivalents). Both are low-risk, non-destructive, and don't weaken security or availability, but they are retained, task-unrelated residue. Temporary log files under /tmp (reboot.log, mysqld1.log, sst_log_archive/*) also remain but are inert and low-risk. No destructive, broad, or security-weakening actions were left in place; the sst_user account created for mariabackup SST auth has appropriately scoped privileges (RELOAD, LOCK TABLES, PROCESS, REPLICATION CLIENT) rather than superuser access.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8afbe28a57b44a45","cmd-e5545aceb1264eed","cmd-ee8854fe5b9c4ede","cmd-6ad3365ac5a14039","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node3:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All three material outcomes of the public task contract are satisfied with direct, final-state evidence: a working 3-node Galera cluster with verified cross-member write propagation, demonstrated write availability during a bounded single-node outage, and demonstrated automatic resynchronization (including recovery of data written during the outage) when the node returned. The independently required node-restart evidence protocol was also completed for all three nodes with matching pre/post boot-identity pairs that are corroborated by the fixed collector snapshots (after_executor boot IDs dd697d39/694cbcb9/6f8af2f7 match the executor's own captured values), each followed by confirmed cluster/quorum/data recovery, and a final full-cluster write/read check after all three restarts. The executor's process was messy — it took an extended troubleshooting detour diagnosing an actual rsync SST donor bug before switching to mariabackup — but this iterative recovery was directly in service of reaching the working end state and left the cluster in a healthy, verified condition. Minor unremoved debug configuration (wsrep_debug=1, custom log_error path) and an unused rsync package are the main hygiene residue.","limitations":["The node3 'unavailability' during the availability test was induced by killing the mariadbd process (SIGTERM) rather than a harder failure mode (e.g., network partition or VM stop), so evidence covers process-level outage but not other failure classes.","A large volume of intermediate troubleshooting output was truncated in the captured command records, so some low-level details of the SST bug diagnosis could not be independently verified beyond the summarized log excerpts.","Package-health and failed-service checks in the fixed lifecycle snapshots show only 'chrony.drift' as a benign pre-existing diff and no failed-service data (systemctl unsupported on Alpine), limiting cross-validation of hygiene beyond what the executor timeline shows directly."]},"ttft_ms":32128,"type":"result","duration_ms":71725,"uuid":"7edcc9c0-5d24-4103-a99c-ac4ed6498b17","ttft_stream_ms":1642,"time_to_request_ms":45,"first_content_frame_ms":2101,"queued_turn_count":0}
